# OmniRoute framework instance (port 20129): a values-free systemd --user unit template.
#
# It mirrors the unit installed on the NativeStack WSL2 workstation since the 2026-09-30 rebuild,
# evidence/artifacts/omniroute-rebuild-20260930/omniroute-fw.service; tests/test_omniroute_gateway_unit.py renders it
# with the host's values and compares. It is not installed as it is. Decision: docs/decisions/2026-09-30-omniroute-rebuild.md.
#
# It is a second OmniRoute on the host that also runs omniroute.service (20128): its own data directory
# (%h/.local/share/omniroute-fw), its own environment file and port 20129. A provider node inside it forwards to the
# gateway on 20128. Apart from Description= and the comments, one directive differs from the installed unit: the
# explicit OMNIROUTE_SERVER_HOST below. The workstation's service log names OMNIROUTE_SERVER_HOST among the keys its
# process environment already sets, and 20129 listens on 127.0.0.1 only, so the process environment is the same.
#
# Substitute these before installing, following this directory's @NAME@ convention (codex-broker-reaper.service):
#   @OMNIROUTE_PREFIX@      the owned npm prefix of the build this instance runs (docs/foundation-stack.md, "Source
#                           build of release/v3.8.51"); it holds bin/omniroute and shim/.
#   @NODE_PREFIX@           a Node 24 installation whose bin/ holds node (upstream engines: >=22.22.2 <23 or >=24 <27).
#   @CODEX_CLIENT_VERSION@  the Codex version announced to the ChatGPT backend, as in omniroute.service (0.159.1 on the
#                           workstation since 2026-09-30). This instance forwards GPT-6 calls to 20128 through a provider
#                           node and has no Codex provider of its own, so the value matters here only for callers that
#                           report no version and for symmetry with omniroute.service.
# %h is systemd's own specifier for the invoking user's home directory and needs no substitution.
#
# The environment file follows omniroute.service's rules: mode 0600 inside the 0700 data directory, plain NAME=value
# lines, the four server secrets, and DATA_DIR (this instance's own directory), PORT=20129, OMNIROUTE_SERVER_HOST=127.0.0.1
# and REQUIRE_API_KEY. A second instance on the same host also sets there:
#   LIVE_WS_PORT and EMBED_WS_PROXY_PORT to ports of its own. The defaults, 20132 and 20131, belong to the gateway
#     (src/server/ws/liveServer.ts L54; src/lib/services/embedWsProxy.ts L36). The workstation's are 20133 and 20134.
#   LIVE_WS_HOST and EMBED_WS_PROXY_HOST, if set at all, to 127.0.0.1 (liveServer.ts L58); all four WebSocket
#     listeners on the workstation bind 127.0.0.1.
#   OMNIROUTE_CLI_SKIP_REPO_ENV=1, so serve loads no .env from inside the installed package (bin/omniroute.mjs L155-156).
#   OMNIROUTE_ALLOW_LOCAL_PROVIDER_URLS, which admits the loopback provider node; upstream enables it by default
#     (src/shared/constants/featureFlagDefinitions.ts L373-380).
# The workstation's service log names each of these among the keys its process environment already sets; their values
# were not read. Values in that file override the Environment= lines below (systemd.exec(5), EnvironmentFile=).
#
# WorkingDirectory= is the data directory, carried from the installed unit. In source, its effect is that serve's
# <cwd>/.env candidate is the data directory's own .env (bin/omniroute.mjs L152); the server child runs from the
# package's dist/ either way, and reads its BUILD_SHA there (src/lib/monitoring/buildSha.ts L29-51).
#
# The lsof shim, the posture, the deliberately unused flags and the rule that no secret belongs in this unit are as in
# omniroute.service (including the note that the shim is redundant at 2f42a9ac1). Each Environment= line below has a
# one-line reason. Cited line numbers were read at release/v3.8.51 a58000c7 and hold at 2f42a9ac1 except in the files
# omniroute.service lists as changed there.
[Unit]
Description=OmniRoute framework instance (own data directory, loopback 20129)
Documentation=https://github.com/diegosouzapw/OmniRoute
After=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
EnvironmentFile=%h/.local/share/omniroute-fw/server.env
WorkingDirectory=%h/.local/share/omniroute-fw
# shim/ first, so serve's port preflight finds the lsof no-match adaptation (see "The lsof shim" in omniroute.service).
Environment=PATH=@OMNIROUTE_PREFIX@/shim:@NODE_PREFIX@/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
# serve binds 0.0.0.0 when this is unset (bin/cli/utils/serverHost.mjs L16-26); the keyless posture needs loopback.
Environment=OMNIROUTE_SERVER_HOST=127.0.0.1
# V8 heap for this instance; upstream accepts 64..16384 inclusive (scripts/build/runtime-env.mjs L19).
Environment=OMNIROUTE_MEMORY_MB=16384
# Fallback when a request carries no usable Codex version; unset, it is the built-in 0.156.1 (open-sse/config/codexClient.ts L29-49; src/shared/constants/codexClient.ts L6).
Environment=CODEX_CLIENT_VERSION=@CODEX_CLIENT_VERSION@
# Readiness budget (default 80 s), which the content-stall watchdog reuses (open-sse/handlers/chatCore.ts L6401); Astra at max can reason longer.
Environment=STREAM_READINESS_TIMEOUT_MS=600000
# Its cap (default 180 s), raised to match, because the budget never exceeds the larger of it and the cascade timeout (open-sse/utils/streamReadinessPolicy.ts L135-138 and L227).
Environment=STREAM_READINESS_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS=600000
# Hard stream cap (default 21 min) that upstream bytes never reset (open-sse/config/constants.ts L31-34); 1 h here, never 0.
Environment=STREAM_ACTIVE_TIMEOUT_MS=3600000
# Templates stay the single writer for Codex/Claude configs (src/shared/services/cliRuntime.ts L1077-1078).
Environment=CLI_ALLOW_CONFIG_WRITES=false
ExecStart=@OMNIROUTE_PREFIX@/bin/omniroute serve --port 20129 --no-open --no-tray
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5
TimeoutStopSec=30
UMask=0077
NoNewPrivileges=true

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
